y  despite his best efforts leaves him for  dead  which highlights another aspect of one  piece i utterly adore  luffy loses on a semi-regular basis like  he can actually lose in a devastating  manner which just  adds so much tension not only to this  arc but the rest of the series and  what's to come in the future  ace's situation for the most part ace  hasn't played a  massive role in the main story until  this saga instead he sort of appeared  sporadically throughout the manga during  specific key instances wherein he acted  as a measuring stick for luffy an  incredibly flashy character  and a component that served to remind me  that all the characters involved in the  story are active during and after their  time  on screen or in the main narrative but  as soon as blackbeard apprehended him  and turned him in to become a warlord of  the sea  ace has become a much more important  character in the story one that now acts  and main goal of the plot and to be  honest ace is a character right now i  don't really know too much about yet but  what i do love about him is what he  means as being a plot device  he is the perfect intersection of all  the main parties involved in this epic  power struggle for supremacy over the  oceans  there's the navy that haven't been  shackled and have invested interest in  taking him down there are the  revolutionaries led by his father  monkey d dragon and of course whitebeard  whom he worked under for a very long  time and because of him acting as a  point of interest for all of these  individual parties it not only serves to  be a great motivating factor for the big  power players in the story but also  facilitates new pieces of info to be  released to us about them  albeit in subtle ways there's a rather  interesting and somewhat illuminating  scene between ace and his grandfather  garp  as ace himself lies shackled in a  maximum security holding cell  in that ace reveals that he's both aware  of and resents his father which is  in